unishment.","j":7,"h":13,"s":5,"a":94,"sd":null},{"k":"5:95","t":"O you who have believed, do not kill game while you are in the state of iḥrām. And whoever of you kills it intentionally - the penalty is an equivalent from sacrificial animals to what he killed, as judged by two just men among you as an offering [to Allāh] delivered to the Kaʿbah, or an expiation: the feeding of needy people or the equivalent of that in fasting, that he may taste the consequence of his matter [i.e., deed]. Allāh has pardoned what is past; but whoever returns [to violation], then Allāh will take retribution from him. And Allāh is Exalted in Might and Owner of Retribution.","j":7,"h":13,"s":5,"a":95,"sd":null}],"juz":7,"hizb":13,"surahs":[5],"sajdah":false}